Third-party code embedded in upstream xEdit
-------------------------------------------

Some upstream units embed third-party code under other terms. These terms apply
only when that specific code is ported. The preferred route is to use an
existing Rust crate instead and not port the unit.

  Core/wbHalfFloat.pas      Neslib.Half, Copyright (c) 2018 Erik van Bilsen,
                            Simplified BSD License (BSD-2-Clause).
  Core/wbMeshOptimize.pas   meshoptimizer 0.21, Copyright (c) 2016-2024 Arseny
                            Kapoulkine, MIT License.
  External/Diff/Diff.pas    TDiff 3.1, Copyright Angus Johnson, freeware with
                            its own conditions (the copyright notice and the
                            terms left unchanged, modifications documented
                            with the modifier's name, free to compile into
                            binaries). Ported in phase 4 as
                            crates/xedit-analysis/src/diff.rs, which carries
                            the notice and the terms unchanged and documents
                            the translation: the view aligns array entries
                            with it, and which entries it pairs among equal
                            alignments decides the conflict status, so a
                            different diff algorithm would not give xEdit's
                            result. The integer compare is the only part
                            ported.
  Core/MSHeap.pas           Windows heap memory manager by Roberto Della
                            Pasqua. Delphi-specific; not ported.
  External/TOM2/TOM2.pas    Generated COM type library import; not ported.

The upstream Delphi submodules (JCL, JVCL, Virtual-TreeView, DWScript, SynEdit,
JsonDataObjects, ImagingLib, FileContainer, vcl-styles-utils,
delphi-detours-library, libdeflate-pas, lz4-delphi) are not ported. Rust crates
replace them. The license of each crate dependency is checked against the
allow list in deny.toml.

Upstream resources carried over into the port
---------------------------------------------

The GUI ships a few files that upstream keeps as binary resources or as data
files. They are upstream's own work under MPL-2.0, and they are carried over
unchanged, so they stay under MPL-2.0 with the rest of the project. Each one
names its origin below.

  crates/xedit-gui/resources/dev_message.rtf
  crates/xedit-gui/resources/dev_message_thanks.rtf
  crates/xedit-gui/resources/dev_image.bmp

    The `fcMessage`, `fcMessageThanks` and `fcImage` `TFileContainer` components
    of xEdit/xeDeveloperMessageForm.dfm, decompressed from the `CompressedData`
    of the form's DFM. The three files are byte-identical to the containers the
    4.1.5q release binary xFOEdit.exe holds (md5 a3493ab32de7c408411696afefe1ba1d,
    12432bf7c116a8964352c87aa44c395c and 0f6d63155516321d857c56c9fd9f6c6e).

    `dev_message_thanks.rtf` is also byte-identical to the loose
    xEdit/devmessagethanks.rtf of the source tree. `dev_message.rtf` is not: the
    loose xEdit/devmessage.rtf is 48,801 bytes (md5
    604266030f66a8d5157c6b5735bbeac2) and differs from the DFM's container in
    more than its line endings, so the DFM's copy is the one carried over. The
    release is the parity oracle and its copy is the DFM's.

  crates/xedit-gui/resources/whats_new.rtf

    The `fcWhatsNew` `TFileContainer` component of xEdit/xeMainForm.dfm as the
    4.1.5q release binary xFOEdit.exe holds it, byte-identical (md5
    f6c29601155ee1a7c23b34094664598b). The container of the source form is
    larger (607,671 bytes, md5 0d255a9980f54ff08dd26d8f703011e4), because the
    release was rebuilt after the source form was written; the release is the
    parity oracle, so its copy is the one carried over.

  crates/xedit-gui/resources/tips.txt

    The `fcEditTips` `TFileContainer` component of xEdit/xeTipForm.dfm,
    byte-identical (md5 5daad2a86321866f330df3c8b3fdd4e0), and the same text as
    the loose xEdit/EditTips.txt of the source tree.

  crates/xedit-gui/assets/icons/xEdit_TES_Icon.ico
  crates/xedit-gui/assets/icons/xEdit_FO_Icon.ico
  crates/xedit-gui/assets/icons/xEdit_SF_Icon.ico

    The three icon files of xEdit/xeIcons.rc (xTESICON, xFOICON, xSFICON),
    byte-identical to the source tree.

  crates/xedit-gui/src/information_text.txt

    The text of the `Memo1` control of xEdit/xeMainForm.dfm, taken from its
    `Lines.Strings` list, and checked against the same list as the 4.1.5q
    release binary xFOEdit.exe holds it: the 216 lines are the same, and the
    file differs from the binary's copy only in its line endings (LF here,
    CRLF there). The port shows the same text as upstream's Information tab.
